PART 7 — PRACTICE: AUTOMATIC SPEAKING PARTNER
==================================================

Build a real-time English speaking practice system.

### Partner Matching

- Automatically find available eligible members.
- Match two members.
- Support audio and video calls.
- Show partner information according to privacy settings.
- Display matching status.
- Show waiting queue.
- Allow users to stop searching.

### Skip / Next Partner

This is a critical feature.

When a user presses Skip or Next Partner:

1. End the current call properly.
2. Stop local media tracks.
3. Close the RTCPeerConnection.
4. Remove old signaling subscriptions.
5. Clear call state.
6. Temporarily exclude the previous partner from the current matching session.
7. Automatically find the next available member.
8. Start the next partner request.

Do not require users to manually restart the matching process after every skip.

### Automatic Partner Fallback

If a partner:

- Does not answer.
- Rejects the request.
- Goes offline.
- Becomes busy.
- Disconnects.
- Fails to connect.

Automatically try another eligible available member.

Use a configurable request timeout, default 15 seconds.

### Matching Rules

- Do not match a user with themselves.
- Do not match offline members.
- Do not match busy members.
- Do not match blocked members.
- Do not match members who are already in another call.
- Avoid repeatedly matching the same skipped partner.
- Prevent duplicate active calls.
- Use atomic server-side matching.
- Respect subscription practice limits.

### Call Controls

- Microphone mute/unmute.
- Camera on/off.
- Switch audio/video mode.
- End call.
- Skip partner.
- Call duration.
- Connection status.
- Network quality indicator.
- Reconnect option.

### Matching States

idle, searching, requesting, ringing, accepted, connecting, connected, skipped, rejected, missed, ended, stopped, no_partner_available, failed.

### Call History

Display:

- Partner.
- Date.
- Duration.
- Call type.
- Call status.

Use an approved, age-appropriate member community. Do not create unrestricted anonymous public random video chat.

